{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;The proposal, by reason of insufficient Gross Internal floor Area (GIA) together with inadequate living space would provide an overall cramped and substandard quality of living accommodation, to the detriment of the residential amenities of future occupiers of the unit, contrary to policies DM1 and DM 26 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;The proposal would result in the additional dwellinghouse being sited on garden land. As such, the principle of the development is contrary to the Harrow Core Strategy of directing new residential and other development to the Harrow and Wealdstone Opportunity Area, town centres and, in suburban areas, to strategic previously developed sites and would therefore harm its implementation, contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2019), Policies CS1.A and CS1.B of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Garden Land Development (2013).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;The proposed two storey side extension, by reason of its overall width and siting adjacent to the boundary with Nos.102 and 100a Locket Road would infill the gap that currently exists and would substantially harm the form and openness of the site.&amp;nbsp;The proposal would therefore be contrary to the high quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2019), Policies D3.D(1) and D3.D(11) of The London Plan (2021), Policy CS.1B of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policy DM1 of the Development Management Plan Local Policies (2013) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
